      timeline: [
        '1900s: Hierarchy games gain popularity in Swedish schools.',
        "1970s: The name 'Kung och Adel' becomes standardized as a variant of 'Skitgubbe' style social hierarchy.",
        'Present: A very common household and party game in Sweden.',
      ],
      evolution: "The game evolved to include specific 'Feudal taxes' where the King can demand specific cards from the Peasant, ensuring a cycle of power.",
      cultural: 'Used as a humorous metaphor for social mobility and class struggle in Swedish student circles.',
