        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to shed all cards to become the King for the next round.',
          gameplay: '1. Standard shedding logic: Play a card (or set of equal cards) higher than the current top card.\n2. **The Tax (Skatt)**: Before play, the Peasant must give their two best cards (Aces/2s) to the King. The King gives back their two worst cards (low numerals). The Nobility and Burghers exchange one card similarly.',
          keyRules: [
            '2s are clearing cards (burn the pile)',
            'Aces are highest numeral power',
            '10s may also clear the pile in some variants',
            'Tax exchange: Peasant gives 2 best to King, gets 2 worst back',
            'Social ranks determine seating and card exchanges',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "As the King, use your 'Taxes' (the high cards from the Peasant) to control the game immediately. Lead with a pair of High cards to prevent anyone else from taking control early.",
          intermediate: "The 'Peasant Revolution': If you are the Peasant, and you have a 2 (Burner), don't give it up in the tax if you can help it. Use it mid-round to break the King's control and jump to the 'Nobility' rank.",
          advanced: "Stalling: If you are the King, 'pass' your turn even if you can play, if you think someone else can clear the pile with a card you want to save for later. This 'baits' the Nobility into using their high cards.",
          tips: [
            'Always know who is next to finish. If the person to your left is the Burgher, they are your biggest threat to promotion.',
            "Keep a 2 (or a 10) for your very last card. It's the most reliable way to clear your hand and ensure you finish first.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
